>
>
"Modern Lojban" is some versions of dialects that are used by some people=
=20
who thinks their own dialects are the modern Lojban, and the others'=20
dialects are not. Here is my "accusation" against the situation.

https://mw.lojban.org/papri/The_egocentrism_of_a_Lojban_community

As for the newer one among the texts of {teris}, however, not only their=20
"modern Lojban" but also my dialect regards it as grammatical.

I don't call their dialects "beta" or "pre-release", but they are a group=
=20
of proposals in any case. There is a schism of Lojban speakers according to=
=20
preference of dialects, and I created a documentary film about it last year=
:

https://vimeo.com/190637628

=20

>
>    - What are (in a few words) the differences between the two? *Why *cho=
ose=20
>    one or another?
>   =20
>
Some of the differences are already described in the documentary film above=
.
I choose neither their "modern Lojban" nor the CLL's, but mine, which I=20
call "Zantufa", because I prefer it. I don't care what the others choose.=
=20
Some people choose "modern Lojban", and some others persist in the CLL=20
Lojban.

=20

>
>    - Where is the reference documentation of "modern Lojban"?
>
>
Unfortunately, I don't find any comprehensive document about their "modern=
=20
Lojban". As for my dialect, here is the one:

https://mw.lojban.org/papri/zantufa

